Say whether a daemon claimed its service, and every event its channel is handed.

TWO SILENCES, both reported only through xpc_log_error or xpc_log_fault, which go to syslog -- and
there is no syslog socket here.

bootstrap_check_in in activateLocked is where a named XPC listener claims its service. Until that
succeeds launchd keeps the receive right, and a client that looks the name up still gets a send
right, to a queue nobody is reading. The client then waits with no timeout and no error.

And a listener DROPS any message that is not a check-in. A client whose first message is not one
waits forever while the server silently throws it away.

WHAT THE FIRST ONE ANSWERED, and it corrected a reading of mine. launchd port-set dump shows
com.apple.trustd as recv=1 active=0, and I took that to mean trustd never checks in. It does:

    CIDER_XPC check-in for service com.apple.trustd = 0 (claimed)

The snapshot is taken at DEMAND DISPATCH time, before the job it just launched could check in, so it
could never have shown anything else.

THE THIRD TRACE IS THE ONE THAT SPLIT THE REMAINING QUESTION. trustd now answers exactly ONE request
and then goes deaf: poke 1 replies, pokes 2 and 3 time out, and trustd is still alive throughout.
That has two very different causes, the message never reaching the guest or reaching this handler and
being discarded here, and the drop trace CANNOT tell them apart because it is silent in both cases.
A trace above the branching can:

    CIDER_XPC channel event reason=1 (connected) listener=1 service=com.apple.trustd id=0x0
    CIDER_XPC channel event reason=2 (received) listener=1 service=com.apple.trustd id=0x77303074
    ...and NOTHING for the second and third pokes

So the listener channel is handed exactly one message and nothing after it. libxpc is not discarding
anything; the message never arrives.
